// Syncthing ignore list for the emu-roms folder.
// Deployed by chezmoi, gated on the `emulation` role.
//
// ~/Emulation/roms is NOT pure content. EmuDeck installs emulators and writes
// per-host launchers inside the ROM tree, and none of it should cross machines:
// the hosts are different architectures with different emulator sets.
//
// Patterns are matched in order and the FIRST match wins, so the `!` includes
// must come first. A leading `/` anchors to the folder root; without one a
// pattern matches at any depth. `(?i)` makes a pattern case-insensitive, which
// matters because EmuDeck ships both `EMULATOR.EXE` and `xenia_canary.exe`.
//
// Prefer structural rules over listing files you happened to notice — an
// earlier version of this file enumerated `/model2/*.lua` and missed the ~150
// scripts one directory deeper. `just emu-sync-check` reports what is not
// covered here.

// --- includes, first ---
// Only this subdirectory of model2 holds games (it is currently empty).
!/model2/roms
!/model2/roms/**

// --- excludes ---

// EmuDeck's generated per-host launcher scripts.
/emulators

// The Sega Model 2 emulator install: EMULATOR.EXE, CFG/, scripts/, *.lua, *.pat.
// Everything except the roms/ admitted above.
/model2/*

// Cemu installed into the Wii U ROM directory (mercury only today).
/wiiu/gameProfiles
/wiiu/resources

// Xenia's own files living in the Xbox 360 ROM directory.
/xbox360/xenia.sh
/xbox360/xenia-canary.config.toml
/xbox360/portable.txt
/xbox360/LICENSE.TXT

// Windows binaries are never console ROMs, at any depth.
(?i)*.exe
(?i)*.dll

// Per-host noise.
*.log
